Sagacious (suh-GAY-shus)
Meaning: wise and having good judgment
Hindi: बुद्धिमान, विवेकशील
Example: The sagacious leader made the right decision during the crisis.
Taciturn (TAS-i-turn)
Meaning: speaking very little
Hindi: कम बोलने वाला, मितभाषी
Example: Although taciturn, he was a great listener.
Voracious (vuh-RAY-shus)
Meaning: having a very eager appetite for food or knowledge
Hindi: अत्यंत उत्सुक, लालायित
Example: She is a voracious reader of historical books.
Amiable (AY-mee-uh-bul)
Meaning: friendly and pleasant
Hindi: मिलनसार, सौम्य
Example: His amiable nature made him popular among colleagues.
Pragmatic (prag-MAT-ik)
Meaning: practical and realistic
Hindi: व्यावहारिक




Example: We need a pragmatic solution to this problem.
Quick Revision
Sagacious = Wise (बुद्धिमान)
Taciturn = Quiet (कम बोलने वाला)
Voracious = Eager/Hungry (अत्यंत उत्सुक)
Amiable = Friendly (मिलनसार)
Pragmatic = Practical (व्यावहारिक)
